LID - 10.61409/V12240886 [doi]
AB  - Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) is increasingly diagnosed in 
      adults. The diagnostic process is complex, emphasising the need for specialised 
      assessments due to the disorder's intricate symptomatology and frequent 
      comorbidities. This review presents an outline for a structured diagnostic 
      process, as is the importance of considering comorbid conditions, as they can 
      obscure ADHD symptoms. It is central to adhere to updated clinical guidelines to 
      enhance diagnostic accuracy and treatment efficacy for adults with ADHD.
