TI  - [ADHD and problematic substance use].
LID - V01250005 [pii]
LID - 10.61409/V01250005 [doi]
AB  - Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) often coexists with problematic 
      substance use, such as harmful use or dependency. In this review, studies 
      estimate a 21% prevalence of ADHD among individuals with problematic substance 
      use, who often exhibit earlier substance initiation, faster dependency 
      transitions, and higher relapse risks. Diagnosis and treatment are challenging 
      due to overlapping symptoms and comorbidities, but integrated, case-managed 
      approaches combining psychosocial, pharmacological, and therapeutic interventions 
      show promise in improving outcomes for this vulnerable population.
