DP  - 2021 Sep 22
TI  - [Adult ADHD - recommendations for clinical management in general practice].
PG  - 1606-1610
AB  - Adult Attention-Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) is frequently found in the 
      general population and it negatively impacts the quality of life of those that 
      suffer from this disorder. Although the general practitioner occupies a 
      primordial role in the detection as well as in the management of this disorder, 
      the lack of training as well as the stigma surrounding ADHD make it not always 
      obvious how to approach the patient with or possibly suffering from ADHD. In this 
      article, we propose to present a few lines of good clinical practice applicable 
      in primary medicine for the detection, diagnosis and management of ADHD in 
      adults.
