TI  - The four causes of ADHD: a framework.
PG  - 391-425
LID - 10.1007/7854_2011_160 [doi]
AB  - In addition to the symptoms singled out by the diagnostic criteria for 
      Attention-Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD), a comprehensive definition 
      should inform us of the events that trigger ADHD in both its acute and chronic 
      manifestations; the neurobiology that underlies it; and the evolutionary forces 
      that have kept it in the germ line of our species. These factors are organized in 
      terms of Aristotle's four kinds of "causes," or explanations: formal, efficient, 
      material, and final. This framework systematizes the nosology, biology, 
      psychology, and evolutionary pressures that cause ADHD.
